# SelectBeaconSDK constraints

Read `docs/development-context.md` and `docs/decisions.md` before changing behavior.

## Must

- Core Location iBeacon ranging only; never add CoreBluetooth scanning
- Single fleet UUID `76F87C5C-AB0C-45C5-8E9A-19DEF7DC2911`
- Identify beacons by UUID / major / minor only (no serial resolution in SDK)
- Observe host location authorization; never request permission
- `configure(appKey:)` before `start()`; configure does no ranging, disk, or network
- iOS 17+, Swift 6, `@MainActor` facade; zero third-party dependencies
- Standard public API: configure, start/stop, non-sensitive `operationalStatus` only
- Beacon / queue data via `SelectBeaconAppSupport` + `@_spi(SelectApp)` — not standard consumers
- 60s observation windows (`bestRSSI`, location, `latestTimestamp`, `observationCount`); close on window end or 30s absence; enqueue on close
- Cached location only; no one-shot GPS per sighting
- Durable actor-isolated queue before adapter notify; only `stop()` bumps `deliverySession`
- Gate Start on `isStopFinalizePending`, not empty open windows

## Must not

- Invent live ingestion endpoints or ack JSON beyond the confirmed payload DTO
- Log tokens, full payloads, or secrets
- Force-unwrap runtime paths; degrade quietly when auth/location unavailable
- Put IDFV / deviceId into AppSupport UI models
